So, after about 5 months of playing, I finally succeeded.  I'm
not sure that I'll be able to write much of a story here, since
I didn't pay too much attention along the way.  Let's see...
I took the branch to minetown, stopped at the town to check
out the shop situation- it was a bones level with only 2 shops
left (hardware and light).  Came back up, cleared sokoban, got
bag of holding.  Went back down and finished the mines.  I was
only level 12 when I found the quest level, but this game had
an abundance of gain level potions, so I didn't have to go too
far before returning to complete the quest.  A wand of cold
dispatched Nalzok without much trouble.

Medusa's island was the Titan version, but since sacrificing 
had produced a very low ac (-46 at that point), and also a
vorpal blade, this wasn't much of a problem.  A ring of levitation
got me across.  Nothing really significant happened after this
point, except for a doppleganger sacrificing accident which left
me at -36 instead of -46.  That was slowly fixed over the
course of the rest of the game (-44 at one point).  I didn't have
a lot of money left over, and all the shops were refusing to pay
me for my gems, so I just gave up on that.

Asmodeus and Orcus took me a bit of time to kill, but all the
others were pretty easy.  Rodney was not a problem at all - I 
had plenty of wands of death and scrolls of charging.  However,
the mysterious force was quite a pain- I think I was thrown back
15 or 20 times as I tried to make my way out.

Plane of Earth was a cakewalk, as was fire.  The air elementals
started to get to me, helped along by an appearance of Rodney and
his cronies.  I finally just decided to blow charge after charge
of wands of death to get out of the air elementals and run for
the portal.  Water was very easy.

The first altar I came to had Pestilence, who died quickly to
wand of death (as did several priests and angels...).  It was
unfortunately the wrong altar.  The second altar was guarded
by death, who I accidently hit with a wand of death that had 
already mowed down an angel...  However, his 5 to 10 attempts 
to kill me failed, and I finally made it past him to the altar.

Here are the details that I managed to capture- I'm not sure which
pieces of this might be interesting, so I'll include it all this
time (this is of course assuming that there will be another ascension
post sometime in the future...):

